export const PHARMACY_TERMS_V0_1_TEXT = "# CompoundIQ Pharmacy Terms of Service\n\n_Draft v0.1 (October 11, 2026)_\n\n> DRAFT, PENDING LEGAL REVIEW. These terms have not been reviewed by counsel and are not ready for acceptance by a real pharmacy. Bracketed {{PLACEHOLDERS}} must be completed by counsel.\n\nThese Pharmacy Terms of Service (the \"Terms\") are an agreement between {{COMPOUNDIQ_LEGAL_ENTITY}} (\"CompoundIQ\", \"we\") and the pharmacy that accepts them in the CompoundIQ onboarding portal (\"Pharmacy\", \"you\"). They take effect when CompoundIQ approves your pharmacy in the portal (the \"Effective Date\"). The Business Associate Agreement or data-sharing agreement you accept in the portal (the \"Data Agreement\") is part of these Terms.\n\n\n## 1. Definitions\n\n- \"Platform\" means CompoundIQ's software, portals, APIs, order routing, payment collection and related services.\n- \"Clinic\" means a medical practice that uses the Platform. \"Prescriber\" means a licensed practitioner at a Clinic who signs prescriptions on the Platform.\n- \"Order\" means a signed, patient-specific prescription for a compounded or other medication, with the patient, shipping and payment information needed to fill it, sent to you through the Platform.\n- \"Catalog\" means the formulations, strengths, dosage forms and wholesale prices you list on the Platform.\n- \"Applicable Law\" means all federal, state and local laws, regulations and board rules that apply to your activities, including pharmacy practice acts, the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act (including sections 503A and 503B), the Controlled Substances Act, USP standards adopted by your state, HIPAA, the federal Anti-Kickback Statute and state anti-kickback, fee-splitting and patient-brokering laws.\n- \"PHI\" has the meaning given in HIPAA.\n\n## 2. What CompoundIQ does and does not do\n\n- CompoundIQ provides technology that lets Prescribers create and sign prescriptions, routes each Order to the pharmacy the Prescriber selects, collects payment from the patient, and tracks the Order to delivery.\n- CompoundIQ is not a pharmacy, prescriber, health care provider, pharmacy benefit manager, insurer or payer. CompoundIQ does not practice pharmacy or medicine and does not direct or control your professional judgment.\n- Prescribers and patients choose the pharmacy. CompoundIQ does not guarantee you any volume of Orders, and you are not required to accept any minimum number of Orders. These Terms are non-exclusive for both parties.\n\n## 3. Eligibility, licensure and credentials\n\n- You must hold, and keep current, every license, permit and registration Applicable Law requires to compound and dispense the products in your Catalog and to ship them to each state you serve, including non-resident pharmacy licenses where required.\n- You must provide accurate details in onboarding, including legal name, NCPDP ID, NPI, facility type (503A or 503B), each state license with its document, and whether each license covers sterile compounding. CompoundIQ verifies each license before your pharmacy is shown to Prescribers and may ask for proof at any time and at least once a year.\n- You must notify CompoundIQ within three (3) business days if any license, permit, registration or accreditation is suspended, restricted, revoked, placed on probation or not renewed, or if you become the subject of a board or FDA enforcement action. CompoundIQ will stop routing Orders to you for the affected state or product.\n- You represent that neither you nor any pharmacist or owner is excluded, debarred or suspended from any federal or state health care program, and you will notify CompoundIQ within three (3) business days if that changes.\n- The Platform does not transmit prescriptions for controlled substances. A DEA number you provide is recorded for identification only.\n\n## 4. Professional responsibility and Order handling\n\n- You are solely responsible for the practice of pharmacy, including prescription verification, drug utilization review, compounding, beyond-use dating, labeling, packaging, dispensing, patient counseling, adverse event reporting and recalls.\n- You will exercise independent professional judgment on every Order. You may decline or cancel any Order you believe is invalid, unsafe, outside your capabilities or not permitted by Applicable Law, and you will give the reason using the Platform's rejection codes.\n- If you are a 503A pharmacy, you will compound only for identified individual patients on valid patient-specific prescriptions, will not compound drugs that are essentially copies of commercially available drug products except as Applicable Law permits, and will use bulk drug substances only as section 503A allows. If you are a 503B outsourcing facility, you will meet all section 503B and current good manufacturing practice requirements.\n- Some ingredients are shown on the Platform with a compounding status, such as \"pending FDA evaluation\". Showing or allowing an ingredient is not a representation by CompoundIQ that it may lawfully be compounded. You are responsible for confirming that you can lawfully compound every product you accept.\n- You will compound and dispense in compliance with the USP chapters your state has adopted, including chapters 795, 797 and 800 as applicable, and will keep your Catalog limited to products you are able to prepare under those standards.\n\n## 5. How Orders reach you and service levels\n\n- You choose how Orders reach you: through your API, through your web portal, or by fax. You must keep the connection details current. Credentials you give CompoundIQ are stored encrypted and are used only to deliver Orders to you.\n- You will acknowledge each Order within {{ACK_HOURS}} business hours, update its status on the Platform (accepted, compounding, shipped with tracking, or rejected), and ship accepted Orders within your stated turnaround. Orders received after your daily cutoff may ship the next business day.\n- If you do not acknowledge an Order within the service level, CompoundIQ may alert you, escalate, and with the Prescriber's direction reroute the Order to another pharmacy. Repeated service failures are grounds for suspension under section 14.\n\n## 6. Shipping\n\n- You will ship only to states where you are licensed to dispense, using the carriers and cold-chain methods you list, in tamper-evident packaging that protects product integrity and patient privacy.\n- You bear the risk of loss, damage and temperature excursion until delivery, and you will replace or refund lost or compromised shipments as your policies and Applicable Law require.\n\n## 7. Catalog and pricing\n\n- You will keep your Catalog accurate and complete, including formulation, strength, dosage form, quantity, wholesale price and availability. You will give at least {{PRICE_NOTICE_DAYS}} days' notice of price increases through the Platform. Orders placed before the change are filled at the price shown when the Order was signed.\n- Your prices must be the same for every Clinic on the Platform and must not vary based on the volume or value of Orders a Clinic or Prescriber sends you. You are responsible for any usual-and-customary pricing obligations you have to third-party payers.\n\n## 8. Payments and payouts\n\n- CompoundIQ collects payment from patients through its payment processor. For each paid Order you fill, CompoundIQ will pay you the wholesale price in your Catalog at the time the Order was signed, plus the shipping charge you listed, on {{PAYOUT_SCHEDULE}}, with a remittance report listing each Order paid.\n- Amounts for Orders that are cancelled before you ship, rejected by you, or refunded to the patient because of your error or failure to ship are not payable, or are deducted from later payouts. Chargebacks caused by your failure to fill or deliver may be deducted in the same way.\n- You will not bill any insurer, federal health care program or patient for an Order paid through the Platform, unless CompoundIQ and you agree otherwise in writing.\n- {{PLATFORM_FEE: counsel and owners to confirm whether pharmacies pay any fee. If so, it must be a fixed, fair-market-value fee for defined services, set in advance in writing and not based on the volume or value of Orders.}}\n\n## 9. No payment for referrals\n\n- Nothing in these Terms is, or will be treated as, an offer or payment of anything of value in return for referring patients, prescriptions or business. No amount paid under these Terms is based on the volume or value of referrals.\n- You will not offer or pay anything of value to CompoundIQ, a Clinic, a Prescriber or a patient to induce Orders, and you will not ask Prescribers or patients to send prescriptions to you outside the Platform in a way that bypasses a patient's choice of pharmacy.\n\n## 10. Privacy and security\n\n- You and CompoundIQ will handle PHI as required by HIPAA, state privacy law and the Data Agreement, and will use and disclose only the minimum necessary to fill and support each Order.\n- Each person who uses your account must have their own login and use two-step sign-in. You are responsible for activity under your accounts and will tell CompoundIQ promptly if you suspect unauthorized access.\n- You will maintain a written information security program appropriate to the PHI you handle, and will notify CompoundIQ of any security incident affecting Platform data as the Data Agreement requires.\n\n## 11. Records, audits and cooperation\n\n- You will keep prescription, compounding, dispensing and shipping records for each Order for the period Applicable Law requires, and at least {{RECORD_YEARS}} years.\n- On reasonable notice, you will give CompoundIQ the records needed to confirm your licensure and compliance with these Terms, and will cooperate with any Clinic, board, FDA or law enforcement inquiry about an Order, to the extent Applicable Law allows.\n\n## 12. Insurance\n\n- You will maintain, with reputable insurers: pharmacist and pharmacy professional liability insurance of at least {{PL_LIMIT}} per claim; general liability insurance of at least {{GL_LIMIT}} per occurrence; and cyber liability insurance of at least {{CYBER_LIMIT}}. You will provide certificates on request and notify CompoundIQ within ten (10) days of cancellation or material reduction.\n\n## 13. Names, marks and marketing\n\n- CompoundIQ may display your pharmacy name, location, licensed states, Catalog and service details to Prescribers on the Platform. Neither party will otherwise use the other's name or marks in advertising without prior written consent.\n- Products are dispensed and labeled under your pharmacy name. The Platform does not offer white-labeled dispensing.\n\n## 14. Suspension and termination\n\n- These Terms continue until terminated. Either party may terminate on thirty (30) days' written notice.\n- CompoundIQ may suspend Order routing to you immediately, in whole or for a state or product, if a license lapses or is restricted, you become excluded from a health care program, there is a credible patient safety concern, a recall affects your products, you breach the Data Agreement, or you repeatedly miss service levels. CompoundIQ will tell you the reason and how to resolve it.\n- Either party may terminate immediately for a material breach not cured within fifteen (15) days of written notice, or if the other party becomes insolvent.\n- On termination, you will complete or properly cancel and refund Orders already accepted, CompoundIQ will pay amounts owed for Orders you filled, and each party will return or destroy the other's confidential information as the Data Agreement and Applicable Law allow. Sections 4, 8, 10, 11, 15, 16, 17 and 18 survive.\n\n## 15. Confidentiality\n\n- Each party will protect the other's non-public business information with at least reasonable care and use it only to perform these Terms. This does not apply to information that is public, already known, independently developed or lawfully received from someone else, or that must be disclosed by law.\n\n## 16. Indemnification\n\n- You will defend and indemnify CompoundIQ against third-party claims arising from your compounding, dispensing, labeling, shipping or counseling, your failure to hold required licenses, your breach of these Terms or the Data Agreement, or your violation of Applicable Law.\n- CompoundIQ will defend and indemnify you against third-party claims arising from a failure of the Platform to transmit an Order as signed, CompoundIQ's breach of these Terms or the Data Agreement, or CompoundIQ's violation of Applicable Law.\n- The indemnified party must give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation and control of the defense, and no settlement may admit fault for the other party without its written consent.\n\n## 17. Disclaimers and limitation of liability\n\n- The Platform is provided as available. CompoundIQ does not warrant that it will be uninterrupted or error free, and you will keep your own process for receiving prescriptions if the Platform is unavailable.\n- Except for indemnification obligations, breach of confidentiality or the Data Agreement, and gross negligence or willful misconduct, neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or lost profits, and each party's total liability under these Terms is limited to the amounts paid or payable to you under these Terms in the twelve (12) months before the claim.\n\n## 18. General\n\n- Changes. CompoundIQ may update these Terms with at least thirty (30) days' notice in the Platform. Material changes require your acceptance before they apply to you; if you do not accept, you may terminate.\n- Relationship. The parties are independent contractors. Nothing in these Terms creates a partnership, joint venture, agency or employment relationship.\n- Assignment. Neither party may assign these Terms without the other's consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all of its business that assumes these Terms in writing.\n- Force majeure. Neither party is liable for delay caused by events beyond its reasonable control, if it gives prompt notice and resumes performance as soon as practicable. This does not excuse your obligation to protect patient safety or to cancel and refund Orders you cannot fill.\n- Compliance with law. These Terms will be interpreted to comply with Applicable Law. If a provision is found unlawful, the parties will amend it to the minimum extent necessary and the rest remains in effect.\n- Order of precedence. If these Terms conflict with the Data Agreement on PHI, the Data Agreement controls. A signed written agreement between the parties controls over these Terms where it says so expressly.\n- Governing law and disputes. {{GOVERNING_LAW_AND_DISPUTES}}\n- Electronic acceptance. Acceptance in the CompoundIQ portal by an authorized representative of the pharmacy, recorded with name, title, account, date and time and the version and text of these Terms, is a signature by the pharmacy.\n"

